  "scalability_blockers": [
    "One A800 was used and one logical workload ran on it; no workload was partitioned across ranks, so no capacity-expansion statement follows from these numbers.",
    "The comparison is cross-framework, and the two sides do not execute the same schedule: CUDA-Q's Python gradient strategy issues one host-side observe call per shifted parameter, while the FlagQuantum side calls one fused XLA program. The gradient ratios measure that difference in call structure at least as much as they measure numeric throughput."
  ],
